  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Adding a low concentration of a reactive element to CoCrFeNi will enable in situ formation of a self-adaptive nanostructured tribolayer.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::webcard",
        "PMC7311485::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed doped CoCrFeNi alloy will maintain low friction and wear from room temperature to 800 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::webcard",
        "PMC7311485::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi alloy is homogeneous and has conventional microstructural characteristics.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi alloy has high friction and wear at temperature extremes.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A minor reactive dopant will act as a second-phase precursor capable of precipitating during sliding.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The dopant will promote nanoscale precipitates that coalesce into an ultra-nanocrystalline surface tribolayer.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::webcard",
        "PMC7311485::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sliding stress and elevated temperature will trigger precipitation and oxidation or reaction of the dopant.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting tribolayer will be dynamically self-replenishing.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A nanocrystalline tribolayer can minimize adhesive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The tribolayer will act as a solid lubricant and thereby reduce friction and material removal.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7311485::webcard",
        "PMC12019924::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective interface will adapt to temperature by changing its composition and structure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to undoped CoCrFeNi, the doped alloy will show statistically significant reductions in both coefficient of friction and wear rate at room temperature, 400 °C, and 800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::webcard",
        "PMC7311485::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention will mitigate performance degradation at both room temperature and 800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
